<title>UK: Pearson off as Capel cuts forecasts.</title>
<headline>Pearson off as Capel cuts forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in media group Pearson fell slightly  on Friday after analysts at HSBC James Capel cut their earnings forecasts  for the group ahead of interim results next week.</p>
<p>The shares were off 4-1/2p to 676-1/2p by 0905 GMT.  </p>
<p>Market sources said the analysts had revised their forecast slightly  to take account of currency factors. The analysts were not thought  to have changed their rating on the stock.</p>
<p>Analysts were expecting Pearson to report interim pretax profits between  43-48 million stg next Monday.</p>
<p>-- Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
